      "writtenOn": "2023-11-08T17:41:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So when created `SkGlyph::fWidth \u003d 0`. So it\u0027s empty before `setImage` is called. So this is more like `setImageHasBeenEffectivelyCalledAfterSettingMetrics`? It would be a lot easier to reason about if `SkGlyph` could only be created with metrics (this class alone enforced that invariant, instead of letting the users try to keep it). I think this is possible now? I think just fixing up SkScalerContext::internalMakeGlyph might work, pass in a skeleton `SkGlyph` to `generateMetrics` and delay creating the `SkGlyph` until we have all the information locally. I suppose I can go take a look into cleaning this up a bit.\n\nFor the time being however, this is fine. I still don\u0027t seem to be able to access the ossfuzz issue for some reason...",
      "revId": "832b1822ab790d2581e6406939bb8a7ecf37de42",
